        <div class="section-title">Part 4: Loeffler's Radiography, Medical Acarology, and Diagnosis</div>

        <div class="question-box">
            <div class="question-text">28. What characteristic radiological patterns are observed on a Chest X-ray during an active Loeffler's Syndrome episode?</div>
            <div class="options-container">
                <div class="option-item"><strong>A)</strong> Permanent, well-demarcated hollow ring shadows indicating necrotizing processes</div>
                <div class="option-item"><strong>B)</strong> Rigid calcified lines outlining localized tracks</div>
                <div class="option-item correct-answer"><strong>C)</strong> Transient, migratory infiltrates showing a mottling and ground-glass appearance</div>
                <div class="option-item"><strong>D)</strong> Complete absence of any identifiable inflammatory lung signs</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="question-box">
            <div class="question-text">29. What is the primary medical management used to control the acute allergic bronchospasms associated with Loeffler's syndrome?</div>
            <div class="options-container">
                <div class="option-item"><strong>A)</strong> Broad-spectrum antibacterial therapy</div>
                <div class="option-item correct-answer"><strong>B)</strong> Antiasthmatics and bronchodilators</div>
                <div class="option-item"><strong>C)</strong> Direct surgical lobectomy protocols</div>
                <div class="option-item"><strong>D)</strong> High-dose prophylactic antimalarial drugs</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="question-box">
            <div class="question-text">30. Which of the following lung-affecting parasites is explicitly assigned as a "Self-study" topic within this module?</div>
            <div class="options-container">
                <div class="option-item"><strong>A)</strong> Paragonimus westermani</div>
                <div class="option-item correct-answer"><strong>B)</strong> Strongyloides stercoralis</div>
                <div class="option-item"><strong>C)</strong> Ascaris lumbricoides</div>
                <div class="option-item"><strong>D)</strong> Schistosoma mansoni</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="question-box">
            <div class="question-text">31. According to medical classification, mites belong to the subclass Acari, which falls under:</div>
            <div class="options-container">
                <div class="option-item"><strong>A)</strong> Class Trematoda under Phylum Platyhelminthes</div>
                <div class="option-item"><strong>B)</strong> Class Nematoda under Phylum Aschelminthes</div>
                <div class="option-item correct-answer"><strong>C)</strong> Class Arachnida under Phylum Arthropoda</div>
                <div class="option-item"><strong>D)</strong> Class Cestoda under Phylum Platyhelminthes</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="question-box">
            <div class="question-text">32. Incomplete metamorphosis (hemimetabolous development) in arthropods is structurally composed of which lifecycle stages?</div>
            <div class="options-container">
                <div class="option-item"><strong>A)</strong> Egg — Larva — Pupa — Adult</div>
                <div class="option-item correct-answer"><strong>B)</strong> Egg — Nymph — Adult</div>
                <div class="option-item"><strong>C)</strong> Cyst — Trophozoite — Cyst</div>
                <div class="option-item"><strong>D)</strong> Miracidium — Redia — Cercaria</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="question-box">
            <div class="question-text">33. What is the recognized common medical name for the arthropod parasite Demodex spp.?</div>
            <div class="options-container">
                <div class="option-item"><strong>A)</strong> Itch mite</div>
                <div class="option-item correct-answer"><strong>B)</strong> Follicle mite</div>
                <div class="option-item"><strong>C)</strong> Storage harvest mite</div>
                <div class="option-item"><strong>D)</strong> House dust mite</div>
            </div>
